WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.599
I'm going to tell you a story today

00:00:01.599 --> 00:00:03.280
about Archimedes; this

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:06.319
wonderful mathematician of whom we know

00:00:06.319 --> 00:00:08.559
not very much. Of all the ancient

00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:10.240
mathematicians we know more about

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:11.920
Archimedes than any of the others

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.120
but it's still not a lot.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.760
But we do know that he made incredible

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:18.880
discoveries.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.760
One of them was in exploring parabolas;

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.039
now what's a parabola?

00:00:23.039 --> 00:00:25.279
That's a parabola; that's another

00:00:25.279 --> 00:00:26.880
parabola.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.880
A fountain creates parabolas; you dive

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.560
off a diving board, you fall in a

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.640
parabolic curve.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.820
And he wanted to know about parabolas.

00:00:38.719 --> 00:00:40.320
Archimedes would never have seen this

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.040
parabola, they didn't have 
algebra in his day,

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:44.960
okay, and they didn't have graphs in his

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.120
day. However this is a parabola

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.640
and it's generated by this formula,

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.360
y equals x squared. And the y-axis is

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:55.440
going up ten times as fast

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.480
as the x-axis is going along. So

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:02.559
y equals x squared. So if x is 10,

00:01:02.559 --> 00:01:06.159
y would be 10,10 - 100; and that's there,

00:01:06.159 --> 00:01:08.400
corresponds to the y. So all these dots

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.000
are generated like that and you've got a

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.280
parabolic curve.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.560
Okay, this is quite remarkable because

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:16.560
it's actually a calculator. I'll 
show you what I mean:

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:19.280
Brady can you give me two numbers

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:22.479
less than 15? 
- (Brady: All right, how about)

00:01:22.479 --> 00:01:25.759
(12 and 5?)
- Okay 12 and 5.

00:01:25.759 --> 00:01:27.600
So I'm going to put a line through the

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:29.759
12, that's it 5 and 12.

00:01:29.759 --> 00:01:32.799
And then we'll put a line through there,

00:01:32.799 --> 00:01:36.960
it goes through 60.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:40.640
5 twelves is 60. So this is an automatic

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:44.479
calculator, isn't it great? Now this

00:01:44.479 --> 00:01:47.040
parabolic curve is set in a rectangle,

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.079
you can see.

00:01:48.079 --> 00:01:50.799
And what Archimedes wanted to know was

00:01:50.799 --> 00:01:52.320
if you put

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.880
a parabolic curve in a rectangle, what's

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:57.520
the comparison between the
area inside the curve

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:59.439
and the area outside the curve? What's

00:01:59.439 --> 00:02:00.560
the ratio?

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.960
He didn't know, he wanted to find out. And

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:04.159
he had a few tools:

00:02:04.159 --> 00:02:06.320
up his sleeve one thing he knew about

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:07.520
was the lever,

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:09.119
and I'm going to make a lever. This is a

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:11.680
normal ruler and I've balanced it

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:13.760
on the six inch mark so it balances. And

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:14.879
if I take a domino,

00:02:14.879 --> 00:02:17.840
and put the domino on each end they will

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:18.720
balance.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:22.239
They would balance if I do it properly!

00:02:22.239 --> 00:02:25.440
They will balance, okay, look at that. But

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:26.720
that's because at 6

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:29.450
inches times 1, 6 inches times 1.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:35.599
But you could do it with three dominoes

00:02:35.599 --> 00:02:37.599
and make those balance by putting them

00:02:37.599 --> 00:02:38.750
there,

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:43.840
and that balances. Why? Because that's six

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.959
times one and that is two inches

00:02:46.959 --> 00:02:49.599
times three. Two times three is six, one

00:02:49.599 --> 00:02:50.800
times six is six

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:53.920
so it balances. So he knew about levers.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:55.680
The other thing he knew about was

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.040
centres of gravity;

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:58.959
he knew the centre of gravity of a

00:02:58.959 --> 00:03:01.120
triangle.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:03.360
And there: I found the centre of gravity

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.120
of this triangle; you can try this with

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.560
any triangle you make doesn't have to be

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:07.360
a right angle,

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:10.400
make it out of cardboard. 
But how does it work?

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.480
All you do is you take the midpoint of

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.959
each side

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:19.840
and connect them to the angle opposite;

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:22.720
and you'll get three lines that coincide

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:23.680
at one point,

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:26.879
and that happens to be the centre of

00:03:26.879 --> 00:03:29.360
gravity

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:32.590
of the triangle - and he knew about that.

00:03:34.239 --> 00:03:36.640
This was found, or a version of this was

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:38.560
found, can you see it's a little bent

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:42.319
triangle. Galileo knew about this

00:03:42.319 --> 00:03:43.920
so it's been around a long time,

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:47.360
okay, why was it on the skew?

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.080
Well I think is because- can you see this

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:51.680
is a parabolic section

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:54.640
here and there's a triangle inside it,

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:55.680
okay.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:59.439
Now, why is it on the skew?
He wanted to show

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:02.239
that no a matter how you cut a slice

00:04:02.239 --> 00:04:03.360
with a straight line

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:06.560
off a parabolic section; if you have a

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.319
triangle inside it or a rectangle

00:04:08.319 --> 00:04:09.040
outside it

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.879
the ratio is all the same and that's

00:04:10.879 --> 00:04:12.080
what he was looking for.

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:13.599
So I think that's why he put it on the

00:04:13.599 --> 00:04:16.160
skew after he discovered it.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:19.040
So I've drawn it again here; and you see

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:20.639
you've got a parabolic section with a

00:04:20.639 --> 00:04:22.479
triangle inside it, ABC.

00:04:22.479 --> 00:04:24.960
So what's the ratio between the triangle

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:26.560
and the parabolic curve? Well I can put

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:28.160
that in a rectangle

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:31.040
which is twice the size of the triangle.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:32.000
Same base

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.160
and same height so it's twice this

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:35.120
triangle.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.199
Or I thought what I could do is actually

00:04:37.199 --> 00:04:39.280
double the size of the triangle,

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:41.199
doubling the height here with the same

00:04:41.199 --> 00:04:42.720
base it must be

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.280
double the size of that triangle. And ask

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:47.120
himself so what's the ratio between this

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:47.840
triangle

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:50.479
and the parabolic section? Or why don't I

00:04:50.479 --> 00:04:51.759
go even further?

00:04:51.759 --> 00:04:53.280
Why is it going further? I'll explain

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:54.880
that later. Why don't we go even further

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:56.320
he said and doubled the length of that. So

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:57.759
we've doubled that,

00:04:57.759 --> 00:05:01.120
we've doubled that, 
drawn that here and now

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:04.160
this triangle: twice the height,

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.880
same base, so it's four times that

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:08.000
triangle

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:11.280
in size. What is the ratio in area

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:12.240
between that

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:15.280
and the parabolic section? Well that's

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:16.880
where he got to,

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:19.199
so where did he go to next? He used the

00:05:19.199 --> 00:05:21.360
tools he already understood about;

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:23.600
he used the lever. So he took the same

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:26.400
diagram and doubled the length of this.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:29.600
I named that point F - why?

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.680
Because it stands for fulcrum. And he

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.639
wanted to make a seesaw balance

00:05:34.639 --> 00:05:38.479
there. And then

00:05:38.479 --> 00:05:43.199
he took a line, just dropped it down, MO,

00:05:43.199 --> 00:05:44.800
and found that that line where it

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:46.720
crossed the parabolic section

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:49.940
he called PO. And he thought about this:

00:05:51.759 --> 00:05:53.914
wouldn't it be lovely if a
line had weight?

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:59.919
Hang on, hang on, where are we going? We

00:05:59.919 --> 00:06:01.199
know from geometry

00:06:01.199 --> 00:06:02.960
that the shortest distance between two

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.720
points is a straight line

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:07.280
which has no width so it can't have

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:08.240
weight;

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:12.160
but he said what if it had?

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:16.400
And what if I dropped every conceivable MO

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:19.199
down this triangle until I blotted it

00:06:19.199 --> 00:06:20.720
out with ink

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:24.160
and it had weight? Now for every MO

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:27.199
there's a PO that crosses the parabolic

00:06:27.199 --> 00:06:28.160
section.

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:30.189
Why don't I take all those POs

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:36.650
and put them on here at the
end of my balance?

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:41.840
Would it balance this triangle that's

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:43.440
still there?

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:45.600
And he said, I bet it does but it would

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:47.680
only balance

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:50.639
at the balance point which is? The

00:06:50.639 --> 00:06:52.960
centre of gravity of this triangle,

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:55.599
which is two-thirds to one-third along

00:06:55.599 --> 00:06:56.560
there,

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:58.720
two-thirds to one-third along there, and

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:00.479
two-thirds to one-third along there -

00:07:00.479 --> 00:07:04.479
point X. And it should balance.

00:07:04.479 --> 00:07:06.800
Which means- can you see because that's

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:08.080
only one third

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:10.000
that's three times as far? So this

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.759
triangle must weigh

00:07:11.759 --> 00:07:14.840
three times as much as the parabolic

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:16.080
section.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:19.280
So half of it must weigh one and a half

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:21.440
times as much as the parabolic section.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.759
So half of that must mean that the

00:07:23.759 --> 00:07:25.120
triangle ABC

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:27.039
is three quarters the area of the

00:07:27.039 --> 00:07:28.560
parabolic section,

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.055
and he was right.

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:34.319
Incredible intellect from an absolute

00:07:34.319 --> 00:07:35.710
genius.

00:07:38.319 --> 00:07:41.680
The quite amazing thing
about this is, well,

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:44.800
Archimedes gave a line weight, right? And

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:46.560
decided all those lines

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:48.960
would equal the triangle and gave them

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:51.120
weight. But what it was doing

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:54.240
was actually inventing calculus; whereby

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:55.360
you measure

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:57.520
tinier and tinier pieces, put them all

00:07:57.520 --> 00:07:58.560
together.

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:00.479
But calculus wasn't going to be invented

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:02.000
for another 2000 years,

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:04.560
and Carl Friedrich Gauss said. oh the

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:05.440
idiot!

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:08.560
He discovered calculus and he let it go

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:09.919
through his fingers,

00:08:09.919 --> 00:08:13.280
so sad. And 2000 years earlier than

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:14.590
anybody else.

